{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792174750,"nonce":"Yum2FyPtSshblR+Jbs/0oHEg/MM=","title":"A String method with an optional parameter, called through Dynamic without it, crashes in --mode jit and raises a cast error once compiled","message":"Reported by the chimpmonk session; reproduced here on the shared release binary (ash 0.1.8, 2026-10-16).\n\nCalling a String method that has an optional parameter through Dynamic, leaving the optional argument out, misbehaves. String.indexOf is (str, ?startIndex):\n\n    class OptionalCallRepro {\n      static function failure(code:String, message:String):Dynamic\n        return {error: {code: code, message: message}};\n      static function main() {\n        var result:Dynamic = failure(\"REFUSED\", \"error SCENE_BODY_SCALE at entities\");\n        Sys.println(\"indexOf: \" + result.error.message.indexOf(\"SCENE_BODY_SCALE\"));\n      }\n    }\n\nResults: --mode interp and --mode hybrid (also with --jit-threshold 1) print \"indexOf: 6\", which is right. --mode jit dies with SIGSEGV, fault_addr=0x3ff808.\n\nInside a larger program (the chimpmonk editor's agent checks, ash --preset application, editor/bin/agent-checks.hl) the same kind of call instead raises:\n\n    [ash] uncaught exception: \"Can't cast (i32 (String,null\u003ci32\u003e)) to (i32 (String))\"\n\nThe reporter's reading: when the method is reached as a closure with the optional parameter, the dynamic call path casts it to the arity of the call site instead of padding the missing optional with null, as HashLink does for a dynamic call; and it only happens once the caller is compiled, which would explain why the small program survives in interp and hybrid. That is a hypothesis, not yet traced here.\n\nWorkaround on the reporter's side: read the field into a typed String before calling the method.\n\nNot started. The jit crash is the minimal reproducer; the cast error needs the larger program (or a caller that has been promoted).","files":null}]}